          "text": "**Observations**\n\n- Spatial extent of W1 structure: the weights are clearly non-random (|w| up to 0.1–0.35) over essentially the *entire* vertical range of the image. Row 0 (inputs 7–20) already shows coherent weights (unit 11 ≈ −0.10/−0.12, unit 14 ≈ −0.11, unit 4 ≈ +0.12), rows 1–6 carry some of the strongest weights in the whole matrix (unit 1 up to +0.35 at top-centre, units 2/3/12 strongly negative there), and rows 26–27 at columns ~5–20 are also structured (unit 2 +0.16, unit 4 +0.20, units 6 and 14 ≈ −0.19). Horizontally the structure runs from about column 3–4 to column 23–24. Only the far left/right few columns are pure noise (~±0.03).\n- The receptive fields are broad, blob/stripe-like regions rather than thin stroke templates: e.g. unit 0 is positive in a tall band at columns ~4–8, rows 5–16 (0.17–0.28) – a \"left-side / sleeve-area is bright\" detector; unit 1 is a big positive blob over the top-centre (rows 1–6, cols 8–18); unit 2 is strongly negative in the lower-left (rows 18–22, cols 4–11, down to −0.34) and negative at the top-centre; unit 3 is a vertical edge in the middle rows (positive cols 5–12, negative cols 15–17 around rows 11–15, ±0.3); unit 7 has a negative diagonal stripe running down-right through the centre (rows 13–16, −0.23 to −0.31) with positive weights immediately to its right; unit 13 is positive in a right-of-centre patch (rows 14–17, cols 15–21, ≈0.25); unit 15 is a strong negative patch left-of-centre around rows 13–15 (down to −0.36); unit 5 is broadly negative over the lower half at columns 5–8.\n- Output layer: unit 0 (left-band detector) is −1.92 for class 1 and +1.28 for class 2, +0.84 for class 7: class 1 must be a narrow, centred object with nothing at the sides, class 2 a wide object. Unit 1 (top-centre filled) is positive for classes 2, 3, 6, 8 and strongly negative for 4, 5, 7, 9. Unit 2 (dark top-centre, dark lower-left) is positive for 3, 4, 7, 9 and negative for 0, 2, 6, 8. Biases: class 8 has a